editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:26:- **The telling on the table** is explicitly a retelling to Oryn of what Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln already established in edition B6: his own Arbiter woke at Kindling; the station plate lit eleven seconds late; the failed-safe word replaced the old name; the Arbiter then went dark. Sources are named by Path, not by person, except the three Oryn has touched. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4, B7] The notice said aloud. The page fetched from the loft and read twice in its counted places. **Her answer** (protected): "So I couldn't read you because…" … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone… I want to be the one you tell." Oryn's new condition governs Tide reading outward: self first, then ask first every time. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4] "You're the colour of the wall…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:27:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
