editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:31:- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets cut to the uprights' heights); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:32:- **New, a learning arc: Lira and the bowman.** The bowman off the gate-walk (unnamed) teaches her to shoot braced one-armed, against a rail and a knee, with the steading's bow spanned for her because she cannot span one-armed and says so. Short sessions, his few words, her fierce economy. This plants the Hall (M8). Oryn's order is kept exactly: the left arm holds nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:33:- **C2, staged:** Oryn decides to leave her mule with the crew. Three boxes and a girl with one arm need it more than a healer whose holds keep beasts. She will take the next hold's beast at Millrace. Her decision, said in her register.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:34:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:35:- **Oryn's window north (111–112):** the spare rope, the road bending, what she carries in her head. It ends before Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:41:- The debt to Oryn (telling her the self-reading) is **owed**, with the day set by her. It is not paid in M6.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:53:Dawn on the 111th: Oryn north on a route seventeen days late at Oxhollow, carrying a spare rope; the crew with her mule, three boxes and a hundred and two in hand. A rule on the page and a debt with a date. Ten fragments and one place that doesn't move. "Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." The completion report has been on a desk somewhere for eight days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:18:First light on the 111th at Thornwater: Oryn gone north, her mule with the crew. Lira is two weeks into the season's order. A completion report sits on a desk west of the Line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28:- **Millrace (day 113):** the wheel heard before the roofs; the ford-keeper's "Five off the ridge" / "I know." **Oryn's table**: fifteen, three serious (a crushed hand, a child's chest, an old woman's knee with a ladder in it) and a dozen small with one hand each. **Ask first, refused** ("You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next."), entered first. Karis: "She was curious about you. Enter that somewhere." **Her arithmetic aloud**, finger by finger. "You're asking me to break the route." / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." **Word sent up the route** by carter (late, how late, why, where to send for the child). **Terms** (protected). Lira's sixth-chair line. The fork log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **The reading taught on the road:** "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes…" Surface at ten: Tide *there*, the first thing that has ever been there at ten. A minute of the long one: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things. "You're built to arrive." / "Yes… That's what I am." "He asked twice and got one." / "That's the rate."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:31:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty-five yards** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Once Cael is within ten feet of the knot, Anchor perception finds it; he then makes the separate purposeful unbinding, without assigning that action a measured reach, rate or price [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:33:- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:41:- Oryn joins as a stop on her route, never as "sixth," never "join." The Stair slip's three hundred is taken and never paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:46:The Lowmarch room; Millrace's texture; Oryn's patients; the road lesson's sensation; the chamber's cold; the stalemate's small human business; the ascent's suspense inside the planted rules; the rim action's choreography; the six hours; both windows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Oxhollow's ford-keeper, the smith, the patients at Oxhollow's table and Teague's crew stay unnamed. Of Oryn's seven holds, only Oxhollow and Thornwater are named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈34,200. **Lira cutaway ≈1,800** (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose before she did; "That was me. The loud thing."). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,600** (days 84–92: out of Oxhollow's gate north on her route, the carter's hand she owed, the child three stops on, the patient she wants to read whole; she decides to put a day on the route; it ends before Thornwater). **Teague cutaway ≈1,400** (day 84, Oxhollow's ford at dusk: four sentences priced before he says them).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈78 per 10k (Tide taught in full; the herd's derived sense; tiers). ≈17 growth beats. Supporting beats for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Teague, Pike.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16:> - The stillhound finding in Cael's hand and its Lira-hand archive copy: discharge sense; slight sight/hearing used for station and testing; water mask; first-mover following; learning. The 110 yards and dusk remain unexplained; two hounds remain open downstream (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:357-401`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:153-171`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:27:**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-05.md`, `chapter-06.md`, `chapter-07.md`; `BOOK_MAP.md` §5 (Oryn and Teague windows), §7 (Tide), §8 (stampede), §10, §12 C7–C8; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 2 append).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:37:- **The Oxhollow slip** (seventy, on the map, paid at Oxhollow) sorts itself to the top, and he counts why: it pays; nobody's finger is on it; it is *ground*. Pike: take a cart ("You want to tell a ford it holds a cart, you'd better have had one on it."). Seln asks about shale-backs quietly at the plank's end, and Cael does not go to listen. The smith's cart is six against its return. The boxes go because there is nowhere to leave them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:43:- **Day 80, Oryn**, introduced through her walk and then her hands: "Who's worst?"; the set ("That's the part you'll mind"); the mend in less than an hour (Lira: "Cold… No. It's going along."); she sits as a carter sets down a known load; "That's one."; "Hands on. That's the only way it works… And I can't do it to me."; Brom's wrist ("Then it should have closed in a month and hasn't, because you've pulled on it."); Karis: "Ember. And nothing. You're empty."; "Hm." at the lattice line. **The first failed surface reading** on Cael: she stops in the middle, looks at her hands, tries again, and her face does the instrument's thing. The protected exchange ends on "That's a *finding*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:51:- Oryn knows nothing of fragments; no deep reading is run. She records nothing and remembers. Her Tide in full: contact only; about three serious mendings a day, fed and slept (two on a road); cannot heal herself; "cannot mend what I can't read."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:54:- Nobody mentions quiet ground. Oryn's other five holds are not named, here or in her window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:59:The bench's days and weather; the herd's look and sound; the exact choreography inside the planted geometry (fin, split, cart, boxes); Oryn's first look at each of them; the walk down; the yard at Oxhollow; which patients come to the table; Lira's and Oryn's windows; humor (Brom's "Carrying." / "Not pulling."; Lira on a mule not mentioning the mule).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈29,900. **Teague cutaway ≈1,700** (days 117–120: following the crew's trail three days along a bearing he does not understand, the healer brought because a shoulder was mended once; sitting down beside the boy; the column). **Karis cutaway ≈2,000** (days 119–120 at the far fire: three copies, the ledger, the edge laid and moved; it ends exactly on the pencil stopping; no who or why). **Seln cutaway ≈1,600** (days 124–128, the road home: the ledger in his coat; giving it to Karis and not asking for it back). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,800** (day 122 to about 128: the gap north-west, four days, three weeks late; Thornwater; the old woman's knee; writing the letter, ending on its four lines).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and eighty-five yards. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:27:- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:28:- **Costs at the track's end:** Oryn's hour, "Twice…" (protected); the long sit, wet to the waist; his bill (Compression in the ribs, Anchor held against biting, the read at its dearest under water). **The exchange** (protected) ending "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:33:- **Home (124–129), on the page:** six days into first snow; the ribs in the cold, then quiet by the marsh's count; **Seln gives Karis the ledger** on the road and does not ask for it back; Lira's taped foot put down flat, the word *ankle* never said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:34:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The cold-term fence** given over ("Ours.") [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]. Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "After the thaw." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:43:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈50 per 10k (the line's mechanics as trials: Arbiter, sigil, declaration, render). ≈18 growth beats. Supporting beats for all five, plus Oryn, Pike, Teague, Ephram, Vell.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:12:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — the Quiet line and OWNER-pending #49 (#49 default in force), binding.]** The protected log entries for this movement stay WORD FOR WORD, including "Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen.", "Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't", "Mine has been asleep since I was fourteen" and "because whatever I am isn't a Path". They are Cael's own log shorthand, and his fourth entry says so himself. Everything OUTSIDE the protected lines carries the edition's canon exactly: at the line the five live Arbiters (Karis's, Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's) stop, at the same step; Cael's own Arbiter woke at his Kindling and has been dark ever since, so nothing in him changes at the line; and his fragments go on answering inside it. Narration and dialogue never say "his Path" or "Cael's Path", never say his Arbiter is awake, working or unaffected, and never explain WHY the fragments still answer. Do not paraphrase a protected entry in narration in a way that repeats its loose wording as fact. The owner may later release these lines; write so that nothing else would need to change.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:16:> Movement 4 already carries the dusk-of-84 location, 116 in hand / six owed, taped ribs, bound calf, new leg, missing right boot, Oryn north, Teague south, nine days to Thornwater, and the three boxes (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18-20`). It must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18:> - The protected shale-back finding remains **derived, not tested** after an uncontrolled two-cause event; twenty-five are seen on day 81, while the missing five remain “heard, not sworn” (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:235-251`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:195-203`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:111-113,341-343`; fix 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:20:> - Karis spent nine points/eight channels for eight seconds and is empty; on day 80 Oryn barred even a spark for one week. She could write one line on day 82 and hold the purse on day 84, but that does not release the restriction (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:41-53,279-301`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:215-219,359-361`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:22:> - Cael's three left-low ribs were broken day 78 and received five bands on day 81, to be lifted on day 99 by Oryn if possible; his reopened calf is only cloth-bound. His nine fragments are held, Shadow remains sealed, and deployment since the Line is one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-155`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-45`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:23:> - Oryn has failed three surface readings of Cael, knows only that he heals fast with no readable current, knows nothing of fragments, has run no deep reading, keeps no written record, and has put one day on her route for the promised whole-and-still reading (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:317-351`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89,137-155,211-233`). Her mule still carries her panniers and covered crossbow; do not spend owner decision #24 early (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-159`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:103-107`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24:> - After fixes 6–9, Teague knows only what his own schedule and the yard/keeper show: he missed Oryn on day 81; on day 84 the five have no cart, have healer-made bindings, delivered a paid no, and all survived. He does not know they caused Oryn's lateness and knows nothing of fragments or the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:237-295`; fixes 6–9).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:27:> - Pike's board has not yet heard the traverse: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up remain the last spoken standings until the marked slip reaches Lowmarch (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-465`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:174-176`). Hesk's letter is still unanswered, Lira's earlier question remains unanswered, and two stillhounds remain open downstream (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-451`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:329-331`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:35:Oxhollow's bank at dusk on the 84th: a hundred and sixteen in hand, and six owed. Ribs taped, the calf bound, Lira's leg new and her right boot gone. Oryn is walking north; Teague's crew has crossed south. Nine days to Thornwater.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:45:- **Thornwater, day 93:** Oryn on the bench at the gate with a carter's hand; "Fifteen days. Since the break." / "Breath stops at it." / "Ninth day. I said nine. You've counted." Her **two reasons** (a patient whole and still for the long reading; the carters' claim about a healer's hands, never checked); "You're a stop. I've added you… Don't make it a long stop." Her table that evening, seen from the loft door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:46:- **Days 94–95, six on the Fallow road** (Oryn on the mule's down-slope side; the registry sheet goes back into the box at the east gate; past Thornwater's fork the printed sheet is white). **The rise:** he looks at the dark place where an Arbiter would be. Lira's hand up: "It's like the air got thick." Brom: "Like a door closing behind me." Oryn's hands half-raised and silent. Karis: "My Arbiter's gone." Seln: "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Five *backs* at one stride. The stone. **Cael felt nothing, either way, and says nothing**, for two reasons: he doesn't know what it means, and nobody asked. The log at the stone (protected). Camp on the road, no fire. The floor takes the last light like water, and Oryn holds her hands over the line until it's gone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:47:- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch10 — OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:48:- **The trials at the stone:** Lira's full burst becomes a step ("It's in me. It's not in the air."; the clock line); Brom's "Skin."; Karis sees every point and can fill none ("It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend."); Seln vanishes for a breath without his Path ("It was never most of what I do."); **Oryn's three crossings** with Brom's arm in her hands ("Nothing in my hands" / "A healer's hands stop working there."). **Cael's two private tests:** the Iron read released before the stride, running across it; at twenty strides a foot's worth of Wind evasion round a stone. From behind it is a man stepping. "It was dark before. It's dark now." Both halves true; together not the truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:49:- **Six over; the site catalogued** (eleven uprights broken at eleven heights; floor twenty-six strides; level under the cord; seamless under his palms, written only as "no seam"; the lip; Karis's chips don't match; the bands "None I own…"). **No instruments anywhere.** **The den** under the far lip (fresh prints; bones in one clause; scat; a hollow worn smooth). "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." Everyone looks at the line and the sun, then at Oryn, then at him. The log at the far lip (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:56:- Oryn reads nobody inside. She has now crossed (with Brom and with the six); her eight solo crossings are M5's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:57:- No stillhound is seen; it is all sign. The movement ends at dusk at the far lip, about to move.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:15:**Read before drafting:** edition Book 6 `manuscript/chapter-54.md`–`chapter-60.md` and the Book 6 STATE_LEDGER AFTER MOVEMENT 8 and AFTER MOVEMENT 9 blocks (coordinator rulings/CLOSED notes) — the seam read; B7 source `chapter-01.md` and `chapter-02.md` (coordinator/reviewer reference only; see the note above); `BOOK_MAP.md` §§1, 5, 7, 9, 10 and ruled C1; `STATE_LEDGER.md`; `universe/UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md` (Edge Territories; Edge Fauna). [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A1; coordinator O3]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:19:The switchback shelf above a valley with no name: the second day past the Line, the second camp beyond it and the first fire. Five people, a cart and a brown gelding with one white foot, three numbered boxes and Seln's locked case under one canvas; Hesk's satchel holds the current log, full old volume, observation notebook, and two no-return-address letters held for a westbound courier. Cael is eighteen, with nine held fragments, one uncounted anomaly, no deployment since the Line, no open injury, and a fading left-forearm bruise one week from gone. “Nothing anywhere was deciding what he was, except him.” [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A1, D1–D4, N1–N4, N7; coordinator O1, O2]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:27:- **Lowmarch, day 9, and the board read like the Cinder House board.** Fourteen slips, not one pricing the crew. Pike: sixties, one arm, "Copper, Force, thirty years on the roads." "Walk, carry, climb, fight." / "In that order?" / "Depends on the day." A heading opened with five names and five columns: Job, Hirer, Witness, Outcome, Price. No tier column. He reads it upside down and looks for the missing column "the way you look for a stair in the dark, with a foot."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:40:- The stillhound's sense is **unknown** in this movement. Karis has the word, not the mechanism; the discharge finding belongs to M2. Nobody hears the words *quiet ground*. No healer, no Tide practitioner, no Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈34,000. **Seln cutaway ≈2,000** (day 97, at the stone through the night and then at the stake: the drawer in his memory opening on maps with holes; it ends as he asks for the carter's map; he does not know, and never learns, where the file is). **Lira cutaway ≈2,000** (days 97–98: one arm across her chest, the order, "Later" kept on her side; walking flat-footed because Oryn said).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at thirteen feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides**. Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln have the sightline; Oryn is screened by Brom and fixed on Lira/Karis, sees no discontinuity and cannot attribute the movement. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B2] The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut, the Iron/body read already released to the air and unavailable under his soles until the lane is relinquished [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B3]; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and thirty yards, back west. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at six feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] From within ten feet, Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:25:- **The hour's mending at the line by lantern:** "There. Back." (she does not mention the clock). The state, said because a thing not said is not a finding. **The order (protected, exact)** and the sling; "One arm. From here to the snow."; "The ankle's a tape and a season…"; Oryn flat on the road. Karis's written lines. Seln: "Nothing." Brom: "Hand." / "Morning. Wash it. I've nothing tonight." The log, including **the Book 9 plant line, exactly.** Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes." / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:26:- **The camp at the stone (night of the 96th → dawn of the 98th):** the unfiled entry (protected). Morning arithmetic aloud: Karis's throat ("Days. Hoarse before it's anything."); Brom's hand ("String… That's two."); **Cael's calf read and not mended**, the fourth failure ("I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."). Oryn against the stake: "Three in two days… That's a route." The route's far end, eleven days north. **Seln at the stake**: the charcoal circle from memory lies on the carter's circle; "Ignorance doesn't stamp iron."; "The Compact knows what quiet ground does. And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." (once); "No… I carried the maps. I never saw the file." Karis: *Where*, then *Entered as said*, then *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* **The contract re-read:** a question, not a recovery; "We just told them."; "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six." The dead hound dragged off and the bolt cut out (five in the sleeve); rations in sixths; nobody says *yours*. Second-night log. **Dawn of the 98th: Oryn's eight crossings alone.** He watches and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:27:- **Two days back (98–99):** Lira walking flat-footed as she is told; the calf closing with no count on the flat by the second noon. **Thornwater:** "Six. Well." Tape off in the yard ("Twenty-one days. A rib is six weeks. These are done."). The calf closed in four days. "Still and whole." / "You don't get a yes. You get told." / "What does helping look like?" / "I'll know."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:33:- Five witnesses to the Shadow use at the Ring and no one else: Oryn is at the Ring but is screened and cannot see or attribute it. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] The pack is not a witness. Shadow is used **once**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:37:- Oryn does not know the mechanism when the movement ends. The telling is M6's first scene.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:16:The second morning after the wall (day 51). Teague's crew went out at the previous dawn on the autumn road and is a week away. The five are thirteenth of thirteen with about ten marks, sleeping in the meadow. Nobody is hurt. Karis holds one word, *stillhound*, underlined.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:35:- Quiet ground stays three sentences from a carter's wife. Nobody asks Pike or anyone else. No healer or Tide practitioner appears; "the nearest walks a route and she's not due" is the only reference.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:7:- Days: 100–110 past the Line (Oryn's window runs on into 111–112)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈27,300. **Oryn cutaway ≈2,000** (day 100, the stool after the telling, the covenant page on her knee; what a healer does with having been a source; no theory). **Karis cutaway ≈2,600** (the week of tables: the tally of kinds she will not say; *the Quieting* chosen because it is the right grammar; **the pen held over the page, and the hypothesis never stated**). **Lira cutaway ≈2,000** (the bowman's lessons: shooting braced, one-armed, with a bow someone else spans). **Vastin ≈300** (the courtesy copy; three sentences, substance exact). **Oryn cutaway ≈1,800** (dawn on the 111th onward: north out of the gate with a spare rope, having left her mule with the crew; the route, the debt she set, the line she tested; ends before Millrace's table).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:12:**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-14.md`, `chapter-15.md`, `chapter-16.md`; `BOOK_MAP.md` §5 (the Karis window's hard stop), §7 (Tide integration; the still place's naming schedule), §10 (Ch14–16), §11 ([UNBOUND] once), §12 C2; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 5 append).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:23:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:25:- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** by carter; "Six went in. Six came out." beside Gault's last note. Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:27:- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets cut to the uprights' heights); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:28:- **New, a learning arc: Lira and the bowman.** The bowman off the gate-walk (unnamed) teaches her to shoot braced one-armed, against a rail and a knee, with the steading's bow spanned for her because she cannot span one-armed and says so. Short sessions, his few words, her fierce economy. This plants the Hall (M8). Oryn's order is kept exactly: the left arm holds nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:29:- **C2, staged:** Oryn decides to leave her mule with the crew. Three boxes and a girl with one arm need it more than a healer whose holds keep beasts. She will take the next hold's beast at Millrace. Her decision, said in her register.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:30:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:31:- **Oryn's window north (111–112):** the spare rope, the road bending, what she carries in her head. It ends before Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:37:- The debt to Oryn (telling her the self-reading) is **owed**, with the day set by her. It is not paid in M6.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:49:Dawn on the 111th: Oryn north on a route seventeen days late at Oxhollow, carrying a spare rope; the crew with her mule, three boxes and a hundred and two in hand. A rule on the page and a debt with a date. Ten fragments and one place that doesn't move. "Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." The completion report has been on a desk somewhere for eight days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:16:First light on the 111th at Thornwater: Oryn gone north, her mule with the crew. Lira is two weeks into the season's order. A completion report sits on a desk west of the Line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26:- **Millrace (day 113):** the wheel heard before the roofs; the ford-keeper's "Five off the ridge" / "I know." **Oryn's table**: fifteen, three serious (a crushed hand, a child's chest, an old woman's knee with a ladder in it) and a dozen small with one hand each. **Ask first, refused** ("You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next."), entered first. Karis: "She was curious about you. Enter that somewhere." **Her arithmetic aloud**, finger by finger. "You're asking me to break the route." / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." **Word sent up the route** by carter (late, how late, why, where to send for the child). **Terms** (protected). Lira's sixth-chair line. The fork log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:27:- **The reading taught on the road:** "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes…" Surface at ten: Tide *there*, the first thing that has ever been there at ten. A minute of the long one: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things. "You're built to arrive." / "Yes… That's what I am." "He asked twice and got one." / "That's the rate."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty meters**: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Anchor let off at ten meters as perception, then as a hand: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:31:- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:39:- Oryn joins as a stop on her route, never as "sixth," never "join." The Stair slip's three hundred is taken and never paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:44:The Lowmarch room; Millrace's texture; Oryn's patients; the road lesson's sensation; the chamber's cold; the stalemate's small human business; the ascent's suspense inside the planted rules; the rim action's choreography; the six hours; both windows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Oxhollow's ford-keeper, the smith, the patients at Oxhollow's table and Teague's crew stay unnamed. Of Oryn's seven holds, only Oxhollow and Thornwater are named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈34,200. **Lira cutaway ≈1,800** (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose before she did; "That was me. The loud thing."). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,600** (days 84–92: out of Oxhollow's gate north on her route, the carter's hand she owed, the child three stops on, the patient she wants to read whole; she decides to put a day on the route; it ends before Thornwater). **Teague cutaway ≈1,400** (day 84, Oxhollow's ford at dusk: four sentences priced before he says them).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈78 per 10k (Tide taught in full; the herd's derived sense; tiers). ≈17 growth beats. Supporting beats for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Teague, Pike.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:12:**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-05.md`, `chapter-06.md`, `chapter-07.md`; `BOOK_MAP.md` §5 (Oryn and Teague windows), §7 (Tide), §8 (stampede), §10, §12 C7–C8; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 2 append).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:22:- **The Oxhollow slip** (seventy, on the map, paid at Oxhollow) sorts itself to the top, and he counts why: it pays; nobody's finger is on it; it is *ground*. Pike: take a cart ("You want to tell a ford it holds a cart, you'd better have had one on it."). Seln asks about shale-backs quietly at the plank's end, and Cael does not go to listen. The smith's cart is six against its return. The boxes go because there is nowhere to leave them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:28:- **Day 80, Oryn**, introduced through her walk and then her hands: "Who's worst?"; the set ("That's the part you'll mind"); the mend in less than an hour (Lira: "Cold… No. It's going along."); she sits as a carter sets down a known load; "That's one."; "Hands on. That's the only way it works… And I can't do it to me."; Brom's wrist ("Then it should have closed in a month and hasn't, because you've pulled on it."); Karis: "Ember. And nothing. You're empty."; "Hm." at the lattice line. **The first failed surface reading** on Cael: she stops in the middle, looks at her hands, tries again, and her face does the instrument's thing. The protected exchange ends on "That's a *finding*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:36:- Oryn knows nothing of fragments; no deep reading is run. She records nothing and remembers. Her Tide in full: contact only; about three serious mendings a day, fed and slept (two on a road); cannot heal herself; "cannot mend what I can't read."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:39:- Nobody mentions quiet ground. Oryn's other five holds are not named, here or in her window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:44:The bench's days and weather; the herd's look and sound; the exact choreography inside the planted geometry (fin, split, cart, boxes); Oryn's first look at each of them; the walk down; the yard at Oxhollow; which patients come to the table; Lira's and Oryn's windows; humor (Brom's "Carrying." / "Not pulling."; Lira on a mule not mentioning the mule).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈29,900. **Teague cutaway ≈1,700** (days 117–120: following the crew's trail three days along a bearing he does not understand, the healer brought because a shoulder was mended once; sitting down beside the boy; the column). **Karis cutaway ≈2,000** (days 119–120 at the far fire: three copies, the ledger, the edge laid and moved; it ends exactly on the pencil stopping; no who or why). **Seln cutaway ≈1,600** (days 124–128, the road home: the ledger in his coat; giving it to Karis and not asking for it back). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,800** (day 122 to about 128: the gap north-west, four days, three weeks late; Thornwater; the old woman's knee; writing the letter, ending on its four lines).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:23:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and seventy meters. **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:26:- **Costs at the track's end:** Oryn's hour, "Twice…" (protected); the long sit, wet to the waist; his bill (Compression in the ribs, Anchor held against biting, the read at its dearest under water). **The exchange** (protected) ending "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:27:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:31:- **Home (124–129), on the page:** six days into first snow; the ribs in the cold, then quiet by the marsh's count; **Seln gives Karis the ledger** on the road and does not ask for it back; Lira's taped foot put down flat, the word *ankle* never said.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The winter fence** given over ("Ours."). Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "Spring." **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:41:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:69:### B2. The first planned Shadow use is visible to Oryn before she joins the trusted knowledge circle
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:71:- **B7 says:** Shadow is first used at the Ring, “circle and Oryn only” (`BOOK_MAP.md:188`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:74`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:22`, `:31`). Oryn does not learn the mechanism until M6 (`MOVEMENT-005.md:35`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:22`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:73:- **Why it matters:** “circle and Oryn only” does not satisfy the term. Oryn is still an outsider when the use occurs, and the current plan gives her line of sight to exactly the tradecraft the seal protects.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:75:- **Amend:** restage the Ring use so Oryn cannot see or attribute it: blocked sightline, attention fixed on Lira/Karis, and no observable discontinuity she can carry west. State in the packet that “circle” here means only the already-informed B6 circle. The M6 telling does not automatically waive Seln's term; if the use moves later, the plan must still establish that every observer either cannot see/attribute it or cannot carry the seeing west.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:88:- **Why it matters:** an Arbiter already dark cannot be observed “not stopping” at the Quiet line. The B7 plan also risks re-revealing to the reader and the five what B6 M6 already established; only Oryn is new to it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:90:- **Amend:** `BOOK_MAP.md:194` → “Own Arbiter woke at Kindling, then went dark after the failed-safe word; station plate lit eleven seconds late.” Rewrite `:279–282` so Cael records only the observable fact: “mine was dark before and after; the line changed nothing I could feel; my fragments still worked.” Do not call the dark Arbiter “awake.” In M6, frame the scene as **the B6-established mechanism retold to Oryn**, with Lira/Brom/Karis/Seln already knowing; her new condition applies to Tide use, not to the pre-existing mechanism.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:186:- **Anomaly count:** B7 keeps the Tide-adjacent anomaly uncounted (`STATE_LEDGER.md:78`, `:80`), matching B6's “still place uncounted” (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1075`). Its later conversion into a felt location remains B7's own planned development.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:231:4. **Repair capability logic before issuing later packets:** enforce the Anchor range, carry the Gold read's medium choice, and restage Shadow's M5 use so Oryn cannot see or attribute it (B1–B3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md:232:5. **Repair the Kindling/Quiet language:** separate Arbiter, plate, Path and fragments; make the B7 disclosure a retelling to Oryn, not a new revelation; revise the protected logs and close (B4, B7).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈34,000. **Seln cutaway ≈2,000** (day 97, at the stone through the night and then at the stake: the drawer in his memory opening on maps with holes; it ends as he asks for the carter's map; he does not know, and never learns, where the file is). **Lira cutaway ≈2,000** (days 97–98: one arm across her chest, the order, "Later" kept on her side; walking flat-footed because Oryn said).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:22:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at four meters.** Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides** (circle and Oryn only). The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and twenty meters, back west. Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at two meters.** Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:23:- **The hour's mending at the line by lantern:** "There. Back." (she does not mention the clock). The state, said because a thing not said is not a finding. **The order (protected, exact)** and the sling; "One arm. From here to the snow."; "The ankle's a tape and a season…"; Oryn flat on the road. Karis's written lines. Seln: "Nothing." Brom: "Hand." / "Morning. Wash it. I've nothing tonight." The log, including **the Book 9 plant line, exactly.** Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes." / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:24:- **The camp at the stone (night of the 96th → dawn of the 98th):** the unfiled entry (protected). Morning arithmetic aloud: Karis's throat ("Days. Hoarse before it's anything."); Brom's hand ("String… That's two."); **Cael's calf read and not mended**, the fourth failure ("I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."). Oryn against the stake: "Three in two days… That's a route." The route's far end, eleven days north. **Seln at the stake**: the charcoal circle from memory lies on the carter's circle; "Ignorance doesn't stamp iron."; "The Compact knows what quiet ground does. And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." (once); "No… I carried the maps. I never saw the file." Karis: *Where*, then *Entered as said*, then *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* **The contract re-read:** a question, not a recovery; "We just told them."; "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six." The dead hound dragged off and the bolt cut out (five in the sleeve); rations in sixths; nobody says *yours*. Second-night log. **Dawn of the 98th: Oryn's eight crossings alone.** He watches and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:25:- **Two days back (98–99):** Lira walking flat-footed as she is told; the calf closing with no count on the flat by the second noon. **Thornwater:** "Six. Well." Tape off in the yard ("Twenty-one days. A rib is six weeks. These are done."). The calf closed in four days. "Still and whole." / "You don't get a yes. You get told." / "What does helping look like?" / "I'll know."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:35:- Oryn does not know the mechanism when the movement ends. The telling is M6's first scene.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/STATE_LEDGER.md:3:This is the entry state for this edition's Book 7. It is built from canon and from the Book 6 close as drafted (B6 Ch23–24), carrying the Book 7 source facts that the opening movement inherits. **Append a dated section after each movement from the surviving prose** (template at the foot). Prose governs plans. Record plan deviations explicitly, and never overwrite canon silently.
