editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:103:2. **The compressed roads and recoveries put on the page (+38,000).** The source summarizes the six days in the fin's lee and on the mountain's lip (+4k); the four days down to Oxhollow (+4k); the six days Oxhollow→Lowmarch (+4k); days 60–69 at Lowmarch and the well on the south road (+8k); the two days stone→Thornwater with Lira flat-footed (+3k); Thornwater→Lowmarch in the first cold (+2k); the three-day bearing walk (+4k); and the six days from the fourth site home in first snow (+5k). Thornwater's three stays get texture as a place that becomes home (+4k). *Why:* the arc's freedom is made of walking and of places that feed them, and the source keeps cutting it to a sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:106:5. **Learning encounters (+25,000).** Holding as a discipline ("the hold"): Lira running without the burst, Brom carrying without hardening, Karis keeping one point, Cael cataloguing his nine as held things with idle rents (+4k). Karis's discharge hypothesis tested (+1.5k). The shale-back study day (+2k). Oryn's field-care and two-readings teaching (+2.5k). The perimeter procedure and the six trials (+3k). The loft covenant (+1.5k). The listening cascade (+2k). The strata demonstration (+1.5k). The reading taught on the road (+1k). The wyrm trials (+2k). **New: Lira learns to shoot braced one-armed from Thornwater's bowman** during the week of tables (+4k). That plants Ch21, where "she could not span a bow one-armed… and could shoot one." *Why:* the formula's front-loaded teaching (§7), and so every winning mechanism is taught before it is used.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:107:6. **Supporting-cast arcs on the page (+12,000).** Private wants and independent decisions for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Teague and Pike, and small beats for the steading's woman, the bowman and Teague's crew (§6). Many small beats, no deuteragonist.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:108:7. **Seam repairs staged as scenes (+5,000).** The horse, cart and purse (C1). Oryn leaving her mule with the crew at Thornwater (C2). Karis pacing the Stair's perimeter on the morning of the 115th and laying the cord at the Hall on the 120th, so that Ch23's "paced two and cord-measured the third" is true on the page (C3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:112:**Do not add:** any new fight with stillhounds before the Ring, which would spend the Ring's surprise. Any Compact face, name, policy, directive or office scene beyond Vastin's window. Any new Shadow-adjacent use (it is used exactly twice: Ring, Stair). Any fragment use in M1–M3 beyond the ford's single burst (the log counts "Deployment since the Line: one" through day 90). Any Daeva or Reydan contact beyond one log line each. Any Ephram, Withrow, Rooke or Bracken scene (letters only). Any Coss, Havel or Ilsev. Any Teague-crew name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:125:| 6 | 38–44 | 36,000 | 100–112 | B7 Ch14–16 (+ Oryn's road north) | Nineteen; the still middle located; the Quieting named; Lira first; the rule written. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:139:**Two hard rules for every window:** (1) **No member of Teague's crew is named, ever**, including in Teague's own head. Book 8 kills "the young one" at the pass and says his name once without entering it. Teague thinks of his people as the spear, the bow, the boy and the healer, which is how a captain counts. (2) **Oryn's holds stay unnamed** except Oxhollow, Thornwater and Millrace. In her head they are what they owe her or what is there: the hold with the child; the hold that gave the coat; the fourth, four days on.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:143:| **Oryn** | 9,200 (3.1%) | M3: 2,600 (Oxhollow's gate north, days 84–92: the hand she owed, the child three stops on, "a patient I want to read whole"; she puts a day on the route) · M6: 2,000 (day 100, the stool after the telling, the book on her knee: being a patient's source) · M6: 1,800 (days 111–112, the road north after leaving her mule with the crew; ends before Millrace's table) · M8: 2,800 (days 122–~128, the gap to Thornwater, the old woman's knee, writing the letter; ends on its four lines) | Her route, its arithmetic and debts; her city and why she left; her hands' findings; from day 100, the mechanism as told; the line's rule, which she tested alone; what she felt in him | Any theory of what he is or why the Quiet does not touch him ("I'm a healer, not a theorist"); the still place before he tells her (day 120); the content of Karis's hypothesis; anything about the Compact beyond what was said at a table; any sentimental declaration — her register breaks once, at the Hall, in Cael's POV |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:147:| **Lira** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M2: 1,800 (day 53, the bar at dusk without Wind: fast, with nothing at the end) · M3: 1,800 (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose; "That was me. The loud thing.") · M5: 2,000 (days 97–98: one arm, the order, "Later" kept; walking flat-footed because Oryn said) · M6: 2,000 (the bowman's lessons: shooting braced, one-armed, with a bow somebody else spans) | Everything she knows (the log, the fragments); her Fenmark and Norhold history; her want; her body's counts | Why Cael's fragments work inside before he tells her (day 110); any escalation of Cael–Lira past what the source shows (warmth and covenant, not declaration); asking for the ankle twice |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:150:**Per-movement secondary share:** M1 3,300 (10%) · M2 3,200 (9%) · M3 5,800 (15%) · M4 2,600 (7%) · M5 4,000 (11%) · M6 8,700 (24%) · M7 4,600 (12%) · M8 8,100 (21%). Book total ≈40,300 (13.4%). The book-level 87/13 is the target that binds. M6 and M8 run window-dense because Oryn is off the road in both, and the windows follow her.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:160:| Lira | To become something nobody has seen yet, with no ladder to say so ("what am I becoming, exactly, if nobody's measuring?") | Says "I could clear it" once and does not; runs the bar without Wind; the ledge; takes Oryn's order and keeps it past the first mile; learns to shoot braced one-armed; instigates the birthday and pays; "Walk away" entered and goes anyway; runs *down* to the stair; keeps the bolt in the bow; never asks for the ankle twice | 18 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:164:| Oryn | The route: the only thing she owns | Comes up a lip because a carter said a crew was late; refuses the ankle on arithmetic; tests the line alone eight times; sets the condition and the terms; leaves her mule with the crew; sends word up the route and comes south as a stop; refuses the lean-to request, grants the road; goes into the water; turns north at the fork | 20 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:167:| The steading's woman (Thornwater, unnamed) | Her hold run straight | Binds four of five; gives the back room to Oryn "always"; "Six. Well." | 5 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:180:**How the first third teaches hard without spending anything:** the log's inventory of nine, with each fragment's idle rent named (Shadow at dusk, Anchor wanting doorways, Storm heavy); the discipline of holding as a skill with failure modes; the board's arithmetic (outcome, not tier); the carters' "don't declare"; the ford's discharge finding; the shale-backs' flight; Oryn's Tide taught in full (contact only, the reserve, three mendings a day, cannot heal herself, "cannot mend what I can't read," two readings); tier talk at the plank (Pike's Copper Force, Teague's unreported Bronze, Lira's Iron R1, Brom's Copper forever). **Cael deploys nothing in M1–M3 except the single ford burst.** The log reads "Deployment since the Line: one" from day 53 to day 90, and the edition keeps that count.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:186:| **Wind-adjacent** | M2 one burst, openly, at the ford (the landing lock with a dog in it); M4 a foot's worth of evasion, silent, twenty strides inside the line (private); M5 two full bursts inside the Ring; M7 on the Stair's rim | The fixed one-count landing lock; never spend a burst near an opponent whose single hit he cannot price |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:188:| **Shadow-adjacent** (sealed) | Drifts at dusk in M1–M4 and is held. **Used exactly twice:** M5 ten strides to reach Karis (circle and Oryn only); M7 up the stair and across the bowl, unseen by the rim, never attributable | Costs from waking; the seal's whole logic is restated once (M2 log) and honored |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:192:| **Tide-adjacent (NEW, the tenth)** | M5 day 100 the deep reading; **the notice** (verbatim, §10); M6 cost: three days of *listening*, not pulling (his own current at the edge of thought; the nine audible as flows); the idle state learned by the third night; **the first self-reading** (a place near the middle that does not flow; location only; not named); M7 ask refused at the lean-to, granted on the road; the first reading of another person (Oryn: banks, one channel, a current that runs *to* things); M8 the second and third self-readings; **"the still place"** (the phrase appears first here); told to Oryn with his hand on her wrist; **Teague not read** | Contact only; surface at a count of ten, deep only with the subject still, whole and willing; does nothing in a fight; *ask first, every time*; "Things you keep touching don't heal" |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:196:**Others' progression:** Lira learns to be fast with nothing at the end (M2), and learns to shoot braced one-armed (M6 → M8). Brom learns Iron Skin is a shout out here, and what he is without it ("a big man with good footwork and a lip of fused stone"). Karis learns to keep one point; the lattice line across a mountain; the wall along a line from her knees. Seln learns that his Path "was never most of what I do." Oryn: what her hands can and cannot do at a line, tested eight times alone. Teague: a column he does not have.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:222:**Injuries tracked forward (no silent healing):** Cael's calf (53 → reopened 78 and 96 → closed 99); ribs (78 → taped 81 → off 99 → the Hall's bill 119 → cold-aggravated 123 → quiet at 129). Lira's right ankle (53, 78, 96; **never mended**); her leg (broken 78, mended 80); her left forearm (96 → season order → reopened 114 → closed; slung at 131). Brom's forearm (53 → reopened 78 → mended 80); his hand (96 → mended 97); his shoulder (114 → mended; reopened 119 → mended twice → bound 120). Karis's palms (53, scars); empty (78); throat and voice (96 → mended 97, voice back by ~110). Seln: unmarked. Oryn: drained at every mending, priced aloud.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:232:**The source's refrains:** Read the source for events, not sentences. It leans on a handful of refrains: "catalogued," "which was a ledger line," "which from Seln was a whole report," "a stride and a half," "the voice for a distance / an inventory," "filed," "the shelf," "did not have a column for it," and "which was, from X, a paragraph." Keep a few as character signatures (Cael catalogues; Pike reads things twice; a stride and a half is Oryn's distance). Thin the rest hard. Protected lines (§10) are exempt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:234:**Reader Standard (outranks voice):** clean language, moral clarity, violence with cost and no gore, no innuendo. Carry the source's Gate-27 WATCH notes into the retelling. The ford witness who "got his hand across his own throat somehow" must read unambiguously as *not* self-inflicted (he got his hand between the jaws and his throat). Name the den's remains in one clause. Blood once, as stakes. Cael's decision to read Oryn without consent is named as wrong by him and by three others before it happens.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:240:Callbacks confirmed in Book 8's closed prose: Oryn's letter and "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." (B8 Ch1, Ch24); "a tape and a season" (B8 Ch1); "Lie still when I say" (B8 Ch18, Ch24); Brom's "Twice… not three times this season" (B8 Ch6); "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (B8 Ch1, Ch5, Ch20); Hesk's "true to a hair" / "draw a line through it" / "Mind the shape" (B8 Ch1, Ch17, Ch18, Ch22, Ch24); "too small" (B8 Ch16, Ch17, Ch24); "Stop touching it." (B8 Ch7); "Not the Quiet." (B8 Ch7, Ch24); "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something" (B8 Ch7); Teague's spring term (B8 Ch1, Ch17); "Eleventh" (B8 Ch1, Ch12, Ch17); "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (B8 Ch7); ninety-six in hand (B8 Ch1); fifty-two sheets and forty-one kinds (B8 Ch9–11). Canon documents quote "Three points make a line. Four make an argument.", "Someone made this pattern.", the looms finding, "A circle is a made shape." and the stratum limit. Every other item below is a signature line or document of this book. **Keep them all exact.** Speaker attributions may be re-staged; the words may not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:252:  [unnamed] — Tide-adjacent. Duration: sustained. Integration: partial.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:269:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. Spring: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:277:- Ch7: *Teague priced us. He's right about the cart. Oryn read me three times and got nothing three times and wants a fourth. Two people out here measuring me, and neither of them has a seal. I keep waiting to mind.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:279:- Ch9, at the stone: *Quiet ground. Karis's Arbiter stopped at a line she can mark with a rock. So did Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's — same line, same step. Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen. I don't know what that means. Nobody asked. Tomorrow we go in.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:280:- Ch10: *The circle is perfect. The stakes are the registry's. The dogs are inside. Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't, and I've told nobody, and I'm going to need to think about why I haven't. Not tonight. Tonight we're inside the one place on the continent where a stillhound can't lose.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:283:- Ch13, the covenant, whole: *Written before. Tomorrow morning, the back room, the door shut. Oryn runs the long reading. Both hands, all of her, all of me, twenty minutes. I lie still. I'm still and whole for the first time in front of her; she said so in the yard, with the tape off.* / *The conditions, as I have them. Sustained: twenty minutes at contact is longer than any bout I've stood. Stakes: I'm three days off the Ring and the nine are still settling; she's three mendings down and her route's late at the far end and she's spending a fourth on a patient who's given her nothing four times. Earnest: she'll do the thing she does as well as she does it. Karis: the model says real, not fight. I don't know if the model's right. Nobody does. Tomorrow's the first time it could be tested and I'm the test.* / *The price. She doesn't know what I am. She can't consent to what she can't know about — not won't; can't. There's nothing I could put in front of her tonight that she could say yes or no to, because the thing doesn't have a name she's heard. I've decided not to tell her before. My reasons are good, and they're the reasons of somebody who wants it, and the real one is that I don't know what she'd say. Entered.* / *If it takes what she's using on me, it takes it from the one person on this road who came to help. I don't know what it costs a source. It's never shown. Tomorrow's the first time it could, and if it does, she pays, and I chose that for her.* / *After: I tell her. In full. On her table, before I'm off it. Whatever it costs me, including the route walking north without me on it.* / *I want it. Write that too.* / *Write it before, not after. That's the whole difference between me and the system.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:285:- Ch14, the words retired: *Still open. Still real. Now I can see it. That's worse. The tenth fragment lets me feel my own currents, and there's one in the place session nine logged, and it isn't the tenth, and it isn't any of the nine. It was there before Oryn. It was there before Brom's read caught it. I don't know what it is. I know where it is now. Patience is over; observation begins.* — and *Daeva's rematch, Reydan's answer — both ride east. Nineteen. Ten fragments. Hesk's package is on a ferry somewhere. The last one said mind the shape. I'm starting to.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:289:- Ch18: *Hundred and thirteenth day, the fork above Millrace. Oryn came. On her terms. She'll turn north the day she has to and I won't ask her not to.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:292:- Ch22, the still place: *Read myself. Ten currents, and I can't find the banks either — Oryn's right. And the anomaly's there. Not a fragment. Not a flow. A still place, and the rest of me has been going around it since before I knew it existed. It isn't the Quiet. The Quiet is outside me and turns Paths off. This is inside me and the Paths — the fragments — go around it like they were built to. I don't know what it is. I know it was there before Oryn, before Brom's read, before the ring. Session nine caught the edge of it. I'm not going to guess. Guessing is what the registry did to me. Observation, then the log, then patience.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:294:- Ch23: *Hundred and twenty-second day, the fork. Oryn north. On her terms. I didn't ask. Five on the bearing.* — *I love this country.* — and the crest: *Four sites. One line. The last one's twice the size and the Compact fenced it. The bearing runs through it and keeps going. Karis says four points is an argument. I say it's a bearing — the kind their maps draw as nothing. Home is Lowmarch now. I just wrote that without noticing. Nineteen, ten fragments, a still place at the center of me, and a line on a map that somebody drew before there were maps. We're not done. We're oriented.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:295:- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:298:- Ch1: "You're paper, aren't you" … "Then you know how to keep quiet. Keep it." — Seln: "Don't declare anything." — Lira: "I could clear it." / "No," said Seln. / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it." — The carter: "First crew I've hired that knew to shut up." — "Stillhound." … "It's a stillhound. You shut up. It went home."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:303:- Ch6: Lira: "That was me," … "The loud thing." — Oryn: "Who's worst?" … "Name's Oryn." … "Tide. Healer." … "Iron. Four, if anybody's keeping a book up here." … "That's one," … "Hands on. That's the only way it works." — "Your ribs are broken," she said. "I can feel that they're broken. I can't feel *you*." … "Whatever you are, I can't read it." … "I've never said that to anyone. Tape them. They'll heal on their own." … "They always have, haven't they?" / "Yes," he said. / "That's not an answer," Oryn said. "That's a *finding*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:304:- Ch7: Oryn: "That's a tape and a season. It'll set." — "Twenty days," … "Round. Two at a hold, near enough, and the road between, and the road's the part that doesn't move." — "I remember who I've had my hands on," … "That's the book. A healer who needs a page to know who's owed has stopped looking at them." — "In the city I healed Bronzes with bruises. Out here I set legs. I'm not going back and I'm not stopping. The route is the only thing I own." — "It's like putting my hands in a river in the dark. Something's moving. I can't find the banks, so I can't read it, so I can't touch it. That's the rule. I didn't make it." — "When you're not broken, I run the long one. It won't read you either. I want to feel it not read you properly." — "Thornwater's on my route in nine days. You'll be on the board by then. Come find me. I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days." — The ford-keeper: "Then they go round," … "That's worth seventy to know before the first cart's in the gorge. I'd sooner pay it for this." — Teague: "You cleared Thornwater's ford with five and lost a cart on the high bench with five." / "Yes." / "The ford was good work. The bench was a cart." … "The board's going to have you and me on the same contract inside a season. Be good enough that I'm glad."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:306:- Ch9: Karis: "Their map has no roads. His has no quiet ground. Between them you get the country." — Oryn: "You're a stop. I've added you." … "Don't make it a long stop." — At the line: Lira, "It's like the air got thick." Brom, "Like a door closing behind me." Karis, "My Arbiter's gone." Seln, "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Karis, "Same stride. All of us."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:307:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A winter either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:308:- Ch11: Seln: "The road's cut." … "The grass. Where the cord went." — Oryn: "Move," … "I can't fix this here. Move." … "She keeps it." — **The order:** "A mend that deep holds nothing for a season. Nothing. That arm is not to hold. It's not to strike. It's not to catch. Not a rope, not a knife, not a fall, not a friend. Not until I say. And I'll say at first snow, near enough, if it's let alone." … "One arm. From here to the snow." — "The ankle's a tape and a season. I've told you that before." — Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes," Cael said. / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:309:- Ch12: Seln: "They surveyed it," … "Five years ago by the stake, maybe six. They paced the circles and stamped the stakes and drew the maps with holes where the circles are. That's not ignorance. Ignorance doesn't stamp iron." — "The Compact knows what quiet ground does," … "And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." — "No," … "I carried the maps. I never saw the file. I'm not going to draw you one." — Karis (written): *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* — Seln: "We just told them. The report goes west on the next ferry. It'll say we came out." — Oryn: "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six," Seln said. — Oryn: "I can't mend what I can't read. That's the rule."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:310:- Ch13: Oryn: "You don't get a yes. You get told." — Karis: "Ephram fought you in earnest and the notice said non-hostile. This is earnest and it isn't a fight at all." … "The model doesn't say the engagement has to be a fight. It says it has to be real." — Seln: "That's not consent. It's the nearest thing to it the log's ever had, and it's still not it. I'd enter both." — Lira: "She asked to read you," … "She didn't ask for the rest. Those aren't the same sentence." — Oryn's twenty-minute report: "I can feel that there's movement. More than one. I can't count them — I can't find where one stops. There's no channel. Everyone has a channel; I feel the banks and I know the Path. I can't find the banks in you. I've looked for twenty minutes. It isn't that you're broken. It's that I can't find anything shaped like the thing I read." — "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something and not known what it was." — "Something just changed," she said. "In you. While I was in there." / "Yes." / "Did I do that?" / "No. I did." … "I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it. You've been still for twenty minutes. I want to see if you can manage twenty-one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:311:- Ch14: "So I couldn't read you because there was nothing in you shaped like a Path for the reading to find." / "I don't know. Maybe." / "I don't know either. I'm a healer, not a theorist." … "What I know is you've now got a piece of the thing I read with." / "Yes." … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone." … "I want to know what you find, and I want to be the one you tell." — Oryn: "And when it turns outward, you ask. Every time. I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time." — Karis: "You have an instrument now. It's not mine. It never will be. I'm entering that I know that." — Oryn: "A stop," … "Good. Write it down before it changes." — Seln: "Six went in. Six came out. He's counted her." … "So has the broker."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:313:- Ch16: Lira: "You told me when you knew. You don't know. So you told me *that*. Keep doing it." … "It scares you." / "Out there I was the thing the system couldn't hold." … "In there I was the only thing that *worked*. I don't know which one's worse." / "The second one. You're allowed to say so." — Seln: "They know something turns Paths off. They *don't* know something doesn't turn off. Yet." — Oryn: "My hands stop at that line. Yours don't. I had my hands in you for twenty minutes and I can tell you what I didn't find, which is a Path. That's all I've got." … "I'm not going to guess past it." — Karis: "We find the others. All of them. And we find out whether they're the same." … "That's how you find a handful. One at a time, for money." — Oryn: "Don't go in without me. Not because I'm any use inside. Because somebody should be outside the line who can put an arm back on." — Brom: "That's not comfort," … "I don't do that. It's a count. You like counts." — Oryn: "Once is a morning." … "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:315:- Ch18: Oryn: "No." … "You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next." — "You're asking me to break the route," / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." — "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." — **Terms:** "You're on the route now. Which means when I say lie still, you lie still, and when I say I can't help you, you believe me." — "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes. That's the answer, and I'm the one giving it…" — "You're built to arrive." / "Yes," she said. "That's what I am." — Lira: "He asked twice and got one," / Brom: "That's the rate," — Seln: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:316:- Ch19: Brom: "Ridge," — Seln: "They can shoot the bowl," … "They can't shoot the stair." — Oryn: "I can see what's wrong. I can't feel it and I can't touch it. Tape it. Leave the bolt." … "the bolt's the plug" … "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." — Oryn: "Ask first," — Lira: "Later." / "Later." — Oryn at the stone: "There. Back," … "The clock started again." — "It held a stair. It's not going to hold anything else this season." — Seln: "No faces." — Teague: "You walked out of the Quiet declaring," / "Yes." … "Then you're not on the board anymore. You're something the board doesn't have a column for."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:317:- Ch20: Teague: "We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted" — Oryn: "What are they" / Karis: "Lines," — Karis: "He tried to drive it. Twice, by the head. It wouldn't go. Nothing goes into this." — Seln: "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another." … "I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say." — Karis: "Forty-one," … "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred meters and a stride, to the stride." … "The floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size," … "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:318:- Ch21: Oryn: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads weight on the floor. It strikes where the weight is. And it strikes what *stays*." — Karis: "It reads that as the heaviest thing on the floor," / Cael: "It reads that as the thing that *stays*," — Lira: "We're going in without Paths to look at walls with a thing under the floor." / "Yes," Karis said. / "Just checking that's the plan." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads the floor. Get *off* the floor." — "You're copying," / "I'm not getting another chance," / "No, I can see that you're not," — *A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest.* — "Brom," Cael said. "Wall. Your weight. Now." — Oryn: "Twice. It'll hold twice. It will not hold three times this season, so don't ask it to" — "You went in the water." / "You went in for Brom." / "Brom's on my route." … "So are you." … "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:319:- Ch22: Oryn: "A still place that everything goes around. I've never felt that in anyone." / "Is it wrong?" / "I don't know what right would look like in you. Nobody does. That's not a comfort; it's a finding." … "Write it down and stop touching it. Things you keep touching don't heal." — Teague's healer: "Twice?" … "Then it wants binding, not hands," — Teague: "What are you." / Cael: "Why did you stop reporting?" / "Because the board pays the same whether I do or don't," … "and the registry doesn't, and I'd sooner be worth what I did than what they wrote." … "That's not an answer to mine." / "No." / "You didn't answer." / "I don't have one. Neither does the board. You said so." / "I did." … "The board's going to need a new column."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:320:- Ch23: Karis: "Three points make a line. Four make an argument." — "That's a healer's sentence," Oryn said … "I know whose it is," — Brom, Lira, Oryn at the first halt: "Twice," / "Twice," / "And not three," — Oryn at the fork: "I'm three weeks late there…" … "I've been a stop on my own route for nine days. I'm going back to being the route." … "Find me at Thornwater," … "Bring the map," — Karis: "Half the bend is twice the round. Four hundred. Near enough. Twice the radius. The same shape, at twice the size, round a thing I can't see." — Seln: "That's not a survey. That's a cordon. They've been here more than once." — Lira: "Twice the size. Is it twice the *anything else*?" — Cael: "Not without her. Not without knowing what a circle twice the size does to the four of you. And not without the map finished." / "It's finished," Karis said. "It's a line." / "Then it's a line that points somewhere. We go home and find out where."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:329:| Integration mechanism (revealed B3; sealed to the circle) | Oryn learns it on the 100th, told in full, the covenant page read; the circle becomes six | Tell Teague, Pike, any hold, the rim; let any cutaway outside the six guess it |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:335:| The still place | Located (M6, unnamed); named as *the still place* (M8); read three times; "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment." | *source, before, primordial, recurrence* (Book 9's word); a Rune-like "shape with bones" (Book 8's); any theory, including Oryn's |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:351:- **C2 · The crew's mule.** From Ch16–17 the crew has "a mule" while Oryn has gone north "with … the mule's spare rope in her hand for the next hold's beast." At Millrace there are two mules; at the fork Oryn takes one and the crew keeps one, which winters in the ferryman's shed (Book 8). **Recommend:** stage Oryn's decision at Thornwater (day 110–111). She leaves her own mule with the crew for the boxes and a one-armed girl, and takes the route's beast at Millrace. An Oryn decision beat; no prose fact changes.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:355:- **C6 · Oryn's lateness and the letter.** Ch12's "The route's eleven days north of here" and Ch15's "nine days late here and eleven at the next" do not reconcile (seams F5a, accepted as spoken). Ch18 projects Thornwater "eleven days late"; the closed prose then says **three weeks** at the fork (Ch23) and in the letter (Ch24), and Book 8 Ch1 quotes "Nobody died of three weeks." The architecture card and `series/THE_FRACTURED_PATH_SERIES.md` still say "eleven days." **The edition protects "three weeks."** Recommend writing Ch12's figure as a distance ("the far end of the route is eleven days north of here") and keeping the lateness arithmetic honest from day 104 (nine and eleven) to day 110 (Oxhollow seventeen) to the fork (three weeks).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:356:- **C7 · Oryn's age.** "Late twenties" (Ch6, Cael's catalogue) against "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something…" (Ch13). With Kindling LOCKED at fourteen, that makes her about twenty-five. **Recommend** never stating her age. "Late twenties" stays Cael's estimate; "eleven years" stands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:357:- **C8 · The Tide stall.** The bible (PROVISIONAL) defines a combat stall that Oryn "has done three times in her life." Neither Book 7 nor Book 8 shows it. **Recommend:** at most one mention, in Oryn's teaching in M3 as a limit she names and hates. Never used, since she is never made to fight. Owner may prefer omission.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:359:- **C10 · The tenth inside a line.** The bible says "all ten fragments function inside." Book 7 shows nine working inside the Ring (the tenth was not yet held). The tenth is never used inside any line in Book 7 ("used on no one" at the Stair and the Hall). **Do not add a Tide test inside a line.** Flag the bible sentence for the canon pass.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:361:- **Already resolved in the prose (do not reopen):** the Lowmarch–Thornwater road is two days; the rib clock (tape off on the 99th at "twenty-one days"); cash 116 → 108 → 102 → 96; Ch23 at the fork is four people and one mule; the sling is "five weeks"; Millrace (EXC-B7-003); the arrested stake (EXC-B7-004); the outer-coping trials (EXC-B7-005); "Twelve weeks" (EXC-B7-001); "two weeks old" (EXC-B7-002); Lira holds Oryn's crossbow from the Hall, not the fork.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:368:**All canon names are kept**, including Bracken in Ephram's letter. **No new proper names are proposed.** The expansion is designed so that every new person is a role. **Do not name:** any member of Teague's crew (the spear, the bow with the limp, the young one, the older healer of no Path); the steading's woman and the bowman at Thornwater; the carters (the Thornwater carter, the carter's wife, the hide carter); the westbound courier at the ford; the ferryman and his boy; the smith and his boy; the landing broker and his clerk; the hide-woman; the crew of three and the mule-named crew on the wall; the ford-keepers at Oxhollow and Millrace; the miller; the old woman with the knee; the child three stops on; the four unnamed holds on Oryn's route; the six on the rim and the second Anchor specialist; the eleven-bale captain and the north-road woman captain. Site names stay descriptive (the Fallow Ring, the Long Stair, the Drowned Hall, **the fourth site**, unnamed). Fauna stay compound nouns (stillhound, shale-back, wold-wyrm).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/BOOK_MAP.md:372:**By-ear watch list for the audiobook (carried from the registry):** Feryn and Oryn never in one list run ("the Bronze from Ardenmere"); the Oryn / Oxhollow / Ostrand O-stack; Pike / Fiske; Stair / (Book 8's) Span. Avoid putting Oxhollow and Oryn in one short sentence where it can be helped.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:103:- A two-wheeled cart and brown gelding with one white foot (B6 ch56:169-197; ch58:125-131; ch60:3-33).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:111:The final inventory is **nine confirmed fragments** in this order: Wind/Lira; Pressure/Feryn; Iron/Brom; Compression/Reydan; Ember/Karis; Shadow/source protected; Storm/Daeva; Anchor/unnamed hand with no face; Blade/Ephram (B6 ch60:203-219). The Session-nine Tide-adjacent anomaly is explicitly **not a fragment**, “came from nobody,” stays outside the count, and remains *Still open. Still real. Patience.* (B6 ch60:211, 227-243). Six people know the cache/falsification history, but only the five people at the shelf know and carry the integration mechanism into Book 7; Vastin knows the cache, not the mechanism (B6 ch60:221-225; B6 ledger:1189-1194, 1348).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:145:Canon is nine confirmed fragments plus one uncounted Tide-adjacent anomaly. Blade's exact notice, tier, range, components, acquisition, engagement and integration are fixed at B6 ch54:145-162; the shelf inventory and anomaly wording are fixed at B6 ch60:203-243.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:183:- **A5 HOLDS.** Anchor's prior purposeful unbinding, uncommanded doorway hold and 10/12/14-foot perception remain entry canon; M8 leaves Anchor in the kit and M9 adds no use (B6 ch31:191-231; ch33:113-151; ch38:341-345; ch54:272-278).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:188:- **B2 HOLDS and is strengthened by the close.** Shadow remains sealed even after the Line because Cael chooses not to test the term; Oryn, before the M6 telling, cannot be allowed to see or attribute its M5 use (B6 ch59:351-359).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:190:- **B4 HOLDS.** The plate lights eleven seconds late, after the Arbiter wakes and the failed-safe event; the Arbiter is not “dark since eleven seconds,” and B7's five already know the B6 mechanism before Oryn is told (B6 ch50:269-273; ch53:101-115; earlier controlling explanation B6 ch36:117, ch37:15, ch39:59-63, 127-129).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:288:- **Cael:** eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments + the Tide-adjacent anomaly**, uncounted, under the standing words *Still open. Still real. Patience.* No injury open: the Crown-yard left-forearm bruise is a week from gone, and the ten-count road bill has cleared. Hesk's satchel holds the current log (about a third of its leaves left), the full old volume, the observation notebook, the sealed Velmere letter, and the held Hesk/Vell letters.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:292:- **Objects:** a two-wheeled cart; a brown gelding with one white foot; three numbered boxes and Seln's locked case under one canvas; the pooled Book 6 purse; two no-return-address letters, to Hesk and Vell, written at the shelf and held for the first westbound carrier. Daeva's reply already went west from the first water beyond the Line. The registry's printed continental sheet and the Ternhall straightedge are in Karis's middle box. Karis has marked the sheet *ridge* and *Shelf; a pine; water at 36*. Lira's separate route book reads *Ridge: one horse, three boxes by hand. Scree: by hand again. Shelf.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:313:- Replace the Shadow source `Seln (B4 Ch13)` with `Seln (edition B4 ch34)`. Replace the final use sentence with: `Book 7 uses it exactly twice: at the Ring, unseen and unattributable to Oryn, and on the Stair ascent, unseen by the rim.`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:350:  `**Read before drafting:** edition Book 6 chapters 54–60; Book 6 STATE_LEDGER AFTER MOVEMENT 8 and AFTER MOVEMENT 9 coordinator rulings/CLOSED notes; B7 source chapter-01.md and chapter-02.md; BOOK_MAP.md §§1, 5, 7, 9, 10 and ruled C1; B7 STATE_LEDGER.md; universe/UNIVERSE_BIBLE.md (Edge Territories; Edge Fauna).`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:352:  `The switchback shelf above a valley with no name: the second day past the Line, the second camp beyond it and the first fire. Five people, a cart and a brown gelding with one white foot, three numbered boxes and Seln's locked case under one canvas; Hesk's satchel holds the current log, full old volume, observation notebook, sealed Velmere letter, and two no-return-address letters held for a westbound courier. Cael is eighteen, with nine held fragments, one uncounted anomaly, no deployment since the Line, no open injury, and a fading left-forearm bruise one week from gone. “Nothing anywhere was deciding what he was, except him.”`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:414:- In `BOOK_MAP.md:188`, replace `circle and Oryn only` with `the informed B6 circle only; Oryn cannot see or attribute the use`.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:416:- In `MOVEMENT-005.md:22`, replace `Shadow, once, ten strides (circle and Oryn only)` with:  
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:417:  `Shadow, once, ten strides. Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln have the sightline; Oryn is screened by Brom and fixed on Lira/Karis, sees no discontinuity and cannot attribute the movement.`
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md:433:  `The telling on the table is explicitly a retelling to Oryn of what Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln already established in edition B6: his own Arbiter woke at Kindling; the station plate lit eleven seconds late; the failed-safe word replaced the old name; the Arbiter then went dark. Sources are named by Path, not by person, except the three Oryn has touched. Oryn's new condition governs Tide reading outward: self first, then ask first every time.`
