editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md-12-> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — the Quiet line and OWNER-pending #49 (#49 default in force), binding.]** The protected log entries for this movement stay WORD FOR WORD, including "Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen.", "Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't", "Mine has been asleep since I was fourteen" and "because whatever I am isn't a Path". They are Cael's own log shorthand, and his fourth entry says so himself. Everything OUTSIDE the protected lines carries the edition's canon exactly: at the line the five live Arbiters (Karis's, Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's) stop, at the same step; Cael's own Arbiter woke at his Kindling and has been dark ever since, so nothing in him changes at the line; and his fragments go on answering inside it. Narration and dialogue never say "his Path" or "Cael's Path", never say his Arbiter is awake, working or unaffected, and never explain WHY the fragments still answer. Do not paraphrase a protected entry in narration in a way that repeats its loose wording as fact. The owner may later release these lines; write so that nothing else would need to change.
