24:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at thirteen feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides**. Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln have the sightline; Oryn is screened by Brom and fixed on Lira/Karis, sees no discontinuity and cannot attribute the movement. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B2] The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut, the Iron/body read already released to the air and unavailable under his soles until the lane is relinquished [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B3]; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and thirty yards, back west. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at six feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] From within ten feet, Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
