Three sentences are added after "Eleven paces above the rock there was nothing coming at all": the bay as a bird would see it (the rock east and west; the arrowhead above it, point uphill, a foot beyond each end; two streams, one outside each foot; shelter between), and then "Cael was coming from the east with a box, so the eastern stream was the one that could reach him; Lira was coming off the ledge from the west, and the western was hers." In Lira's window "the right-hand stream" is now "the western stream" (ch19:309). Nothing is shortened; the pricing of Compression and Anchor is as it was.

