+
+## (4) Reader clarity
+
+Speaker attribution is stable throughout the repair. Oryn's arrival now has a clean carrier sequence (Lira hears, Seln reports, Oryn appears); the failed reading keeps body and hand positions explicit; the ankle request clearly precedes the examination. The new overhead paragraph makes east/west, the rock, the arrowhead, both streams and both runners trackable through a 13-year-old lens. `heard, not sworn` now has a concrete casualty antecedent. The day-84 reset and Oryn's day-by-day sum remove both calendar traps.
+
+The remaining referent defect is in ch16: `a foot as broad as that` has no narrated `that`. A print reader may infer a gesture; a listener receives an empty demonstrative. The one-line addition below supplies the missing action while preserving the new footmark, its uncertainty and its source distance. With that fix, Reader Standard passes.
+
+## (5) Listening proof
+
+I read every chapter aloud-by-ear after the diff review, including all changed joins. Raw straight-quote and asterisk delimiters are even in every file (ch15 180 / 20; ch16 178 / 16; ch17 246 / 18; ch18 116 / 26; ch19 68 / 32; ch20 268 / 18; ch21 294 / 6; ch22 116 / 20). Every `---` separator is isolated with blank space. No prose numeral or narrator-facing abbreviation produces a misvoice. Context distinguishes `read`, proper-Path `Wind` from ordinary wind, the cart's `bow` from Teague's bow-role, and duration `minute`; no unresolved homograph or Oryn/Oxhollow ear collision remains.
+
+| Chapter | Listening result |
+|---|---|
+| 15 | **PASS.** Board arithmetic, the three reasons, cart terms and the transition onto the traverse retain clear speakers and antecedents after compression. |
+| 16 | **LINE FIX.** Procedure joins, Seln's announced departure and the pebble sequence read cleanly. The new seep speech has one inaudible visual referent, `as broad as that`; fix 1 supplies its missing gesture. |
+| 17 | **PASS.** The compressed fire test and observation day preserve cause, speaker and time order; `Derived. Not tested.` lands on its stated evidence. |
+| 18 | **PASS.** The compressed narrowings still advance numerically and spatially; the removed scene break creates no false time jump or broken join. |
+| 19 | **PASS.** The added bird's-eye orientation reads as one coherent reset before the two streams; east/west remains stable in Lira's window. |
+| 20 | **PASS.** Sound → Seln → Oryn is easy to hear; the restored Cold unit is exact; the hand that remains, the wrist check and the hand that returns are unambiguous. |
+| 21 | **PASS.** `He found the edge` has an immediate tape antecedent; the walk-before-halt ankle sequence is chronological; the Tide axiom is exact and naturally attributed. |
