+## (2) Continuity
+
+**Entry and exit.** Chapter 15 opens on day 70 after Movement 2's day-69 Lowmarch close. The main action reaches Oxhollow on day 84; Oryn's window alone looks forward through day 92; the explicit reset returns to day 84. Movement 4 can therefore open at Oxhollow at dusk on day 84. The route arithmetic above reaches Thornwater on days 93 and 99 and the deep reading on day 100 exactly as Movements 4–5 and the BOOK_MAP require.
+
+**Counts, bodies, money and objects.** Cael remains eighteen; `nineteen` does not appear. Nine fragments remain confirmed, Shadow remains sealed, and every deployment log says `Deployment since the Line: one.` No fragment is used on the mountain. The herd finding remains derived, not tested. Lira's tibia is mended/new; her ankle is explicitly `taped and will not be mended`. Cael's calf is bound, not mended; the ribs are taped for twenty-one days. Brom's wrist restrictions, Karis's depletion, 116 in hand / six owed, the three recovered boxes, surviving bill and ash wedge, lost cart/load and unpriced rope obligation all agree with the entry state and Movement 4 inheritance.
+
+**Oryn's knowledge boundary.** Oryn runs three surface readings and no deep reading. She knows nothing of fragments; all fragment references occur outside her knowledge. `More than one` is absent. She records nothing, names the stall once, and knows only movement without readable banks. Nobody in the movement mentions quiet ground. The protected Cold sentence appears once, verbatim: `Lira's face went a colour that was not white, and she said "Cold," not to anyone, and then "No. It's going along," and put her head back and shut her eyes.` The Tide axiom also appears once, verbatim: `Because I cannot mend what I can't read.` No proposed fix touches either protected unit.
+
+**Teague's complete window — PASS.** On the hill Oryn tells him only `I was late.` His own schedule tells him that she missed the upper hold; it does not tell him why. From the yard he can read no cart, three boxes on the ground, healer-made bindings, a strapped bare foot, a boy holding his side, a delivered map, five survivors and the keeper's price. The narration itself closes the boundary: `there was nothing in it that a man could not have read off a yard and a keeper.` He never connects the lost day or the bow's hip to the five; `The healer's lateness was not theirs on any ground he had read.` passes exactly.
+
+**Clawless footmark — KEEP.** It is an unconfirmed sign, not a named species or a new mechanism. `Heavy`, broad-footed and clawless is compatible with the bible's cart-sized armored shale-backs, but the text correctly does not identify it. It does not contradict the later packets' stillhound prints at the Ring or any reserved Edge Fauna truth, and its absence from the source confirms that it is not new tracking. Keep the canon beat. The sole issue is that its spoken width currently depends on an unnarrated gesture; the exact line fix below makes the referent audible without naming the animal or fixing a measurement.
+
+**Owner rulings.** The movement remains season-blind, uses feet/yards/paces, gives no elapsed-year count since Kindling, does not call any fragment set Cael's Path, preserves the Book 6 handoff, does not spend the future mule transfer, and does not anticipate the protected Quiet-line or Seln-duration questions. OWNER-DECISIONS #18, #23, #24, #42, #46, #48, #49 and #50 therefore remain intact.
+
+**Ledger hygiene at close.** Two stale statements should be corrected when the coordinator closes the movement: the Movement 3 coordinator bullet saying `Cael's calf is MENDED (the leg)` conflicts with the exact state and next-movement inheritance, both of which correctly say cloth-bound and not mended; and the `New canon minted` Teague flag still quotes the deleted `They're not mine` / `not anybody's` exchange. The binding coordinator rulings, surviving prose and packet inheritance are unambiguous, so these are administrative remnants, not manuscript failures.
